        "original_id": "4a29e10b-483f-5b5f-8e52-b4208f4fbca9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Die Rhöner Säuwäntzt, The Vipers Skiffle Group\n- People: Lonnie Donegan, Ken Colyer, Chas McDevitt\n- Places: Eichenzell-Lütter, Hessen, Germany, United States, United Kingdom\n- Concepts: Skiffle, Skiffle-Bluesband\n\nFacts:\n- In the first half of the 20th century, skiffle originated as a term in the United States.\n- In the 1950s, skiffle became popular again in the United Kingdom.\n- In the 1950s, skiffle in the United Kingdom was associated with Lonnie Donegan, The Vipers Skiffle Group, Ken Colyer, and Chas McDevitt.\n- Die Rhöner Säuwäntzt are a skiffle-blues band from Eichenzell-Lütter in Hessen, Germany.",
